  "intro": {
    "title": "Zwei Kilo Äpfel",
    "paragraphs": [
      "With numbers, measure words stay singular: zwei Euro, drei Kilo, fünf Meter, zwanzig Grad. And you don't need 'of': ein Kilo Äpfel is a kilo of apples.",
      "Germans use the metric system. At the market a Pfund is exactly 500 grams. Prices are said with Euro in the middle: 2,50 € is zwei Euro fünfzig."
    ]
  },
